This is the exact, machine-generated API: both halves of it produced from the same
Zig declarations the library compiles, so neither can drift away from the code it
describes. For *which* surface to reach for and how to start, see
[Surfaces]($link.page('surfaces')); this page is the lookup.

## The Zig API

The [Zig API reference]($link.page('reference/api')) is generated from the public
`pancake` module on every site build. It is the exact surface a Zig consumer imports,
with the ownership and lifetime notes attached to the declarations that carry them.

## The C ABI

The C surface is a set of composable archives with one header each. The base is
[`pancake_ocapn.h`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/include/pancake_ocapn.h)
for `libpancake_ocapn`, with `pancake_net_transport_tcp.h` and `pancake_net_transport_inproc.h` for the
transport archives; each is generated from the same Zig declarations, so a header and
its archive can never silently disagree. The optional iroh transport adds
[`pancake_net_transport_iroh.h`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/include/pancake_net_transport_iroh.h)
as a companion (it `#include`s `pancake_ocapn.h` and adds only the `pancake_iroh_*`
family; link it alongside the core archives). For the route from a build to a first complete C program, read
[consuming pancake from C](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/consuming-from-c.md).
